// Chronicle rules: the activities
// -------------------------------
// The script the game loads. Everything is in activitytable.pg, which says what goes in and what
// comes out: this file only imports it.
//
// Loading a script leaves its bytecode beside it (activities.pgc), and a script that imports a
// module with a .pgc beside it gets that bytecode instead of the source: an engine path that
// does not compile here (windows.pg importing a compiled activities) and that would not follow
// an edit either. So what the other scripts import (activitytable) is never loaded itself, and
// what is loaded (activities) is never imported.

import "string"
import "math"
import "algorithm"
import "activitytable"
